------------------
---- MONITORS ----
------------------

-- See https://wiki.hypr.land/Configuring/Basics/Monitors/
-- Explicit coordinates, not "auto".
--
-- `auto`/`auto-right` place monitors in enumeration order, and that order
-- depends on which GPU is primary. Making the dGPU primary for gaming flipped
-- it: HDMI-A-2 landed at 0,0 and the laptop panel ended up on the *right*,
-- so moving the cursor left off the big screen hit nothing.
--
-- eDP-1 is 1920x1080 at scale 1.5, i.e. 1280x720 logical — so HDMI-A-2
-- starts at x=1280, immediately to its right. Layout is now fixed regardless
-- of GPU order or plug-in sequence.
hl.monitor({
    output   = "eDP-1",
    mode     = "1920x1080@360",
    position = "0x0",
    scale    = 1.5,
})

hl.monitor({
    output   = "HDMI-A-2",
    mode     = "2560x1440@144",
    position = "1280x0",
    scale    = 1,
})

